CatTunnel for routers

Part of CatTunnel (https://github.com/Cattunnel/cattunnel), a VPN client for
TrustTunnel servers based on TrustTunnel by AdGuard. Licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). The changes and additions by the CatTunnel
authors are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 as well.

The packages built from this repository bundle:

- trusttunnel_client, built from https://github.com/TrustTunnel/TrustTunnelClient
  (Copyright Adguard Software Ltd, Apache License 2.0) with
  engine/0001-anti-dpi-desync.patch. The anti-DPI techniques in that patch
  (out-of-band byte, TTL-1 piece, split positions, custom-string syntax) are
  adapted from ByeDPI (https://github.com/hufrea/byedpi), Copyright (c) 2024
  hufrea, MIT License.
- engine/*.patch for NativeLibsCommon and DnsLibs (AdGuard, Apache-2.0):
  build fixes only.
- age (https://github.com/FiloSottile/age), Copyright 2019 The age Authors and
  Google LLC, BSD 3-Clause License.

The license files of the engine and of age are installed with the package
(/usr/share/doc/cattunnel/). shared/ holds copies of files from the main
CatTunnel repository (Russian services list, "how the connection works" help);
keys/ holds the public release key and the signing helper.
